WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.196
In March 1908 the Hope family crossed the

2
00:00:03.196 --> 00:00:06.093
Atlantic from England to Cleveland, Ohio.

3
00:00:06.443 --> 00:00:10.623
Among the seven sons was a four-year-old named Leslie Townes Hope.

4
00:00:10.973 --> 00:00:14.871
Hope went into vaudeville in 1922, worked up through

5
00:00:14.871 --> 00:00:18.769
partner acts and Broadway revues, and in 1928 struck

6
00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:23.117
out as a solo comedian — changing his first name to "Bob."

7
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:28.097
He took his radio show overseas in 1943, began his Christmas

8
00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:32.419
shows for the troops in 1948, and performed for American

9
00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:37.898
servicemen and women through the Korean War, Vietnam, and the Gulf War.

10
00:00:38.248 --> 00:00:40.930
Hope never took a citizenship oath of his own.

11
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.721
The boy who had crossed the Atlantic at four was

12
00:00:43.721 --> 00:00:46.365
made an American by an act in which he took no part.

13
00:00:46.715 --> 00:00:49.687
Read the full story, with every source, on this page.
